  <prompt>Implement the H12c runtime references handler as an IJobHandler in the L2 control plane per spec.md FR-17. H12c populates sprk_aimodeldeployment rows (placeholders seeded by H12a) with real endpoint URIs: for Model 2 (dedicated stamp) → customer's OpenAI endpoint from H2a; for Model 1 (shared tier) → shared platform OpenAI with per-tenant metering attribution wired. Idempotency key: h12c-{customerId}-{tenancyModel}-{endpointHash}.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in IJobHandler contract (ADR-004), Dataverse alternate-key upsert, Azure OpenAI endpoint discovery via ARM, sprk_aimodeldeployment schema, and Model 1/2 tier-branching per §4.1a. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>File src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H12cRuntimeReferencesHandler.cs exists, implements IJobHandler, registers in L2 DI, and: (a) reads sprk_dataverseenvironment.sprk_tenancymodel; (b) for Model 2, reads customer OpenAI endpoint from H2a-provisioned resource; (c) for Model 1, reads shared platform OpenAI endpoint + wires per-tenant metering attribution (task 077); (d) upserts sprk_aimodeldeployment rows with endpoint URI values; (e) asserts idempotency. Unit tests cover Model 1, Model 2, and idempotency paths.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Per spec.md FR-17 + §4.1a Model 1 vs Model 2 handler-differences table + design.md §4.1 H12c row: H12a seeded sprk_aimodeldeployment PLACEHOLDER rows. H12c populates them with real endpoint URIs. Tier determines the endpoint source: Model 2 uses the customer's dedicated OpenAI (from H2a); Model 1 uses shared platform OpenAI with per-tenant metering keyed on tenantId (task 077). BFF's AzureOpenAIOptions.Endpoint resolves via env-var lookup + sprk_aimodeldeployment join — so H12c is the last mile that makes AI actually work per customer.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H12cRuntimeReferencesHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H12cRuntimeReferencesHandler.Tests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Program.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/IdempotencyService.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="044" status="pending">H2a Bicep infra deploy — provides customer OpenAI endpoint for Model 2</dependency>
      <dependency task="070" status="pending">H12a seeded sprk_aimodeldeployment placeholder rows</dependency>
      <dependency task="071" status="pending">H12b app-config seed complete (no direct dep but DAG placement follows both)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-17">SCOPE: sprk_aimodeldeployment rows point at correct OpenAI endpoint per tenancy tier; BFF AzureOpenAIOptions.Endpoint resolves via env-var lookup + join.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §4.1a">SCOPE: Model 1 uses shared platform OpenAI with per-tenant metering; Model 2 uses dedicated customer OpenAI from H2a.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">SCOPE: Single IJobHandler; one message, one handler, one outcome.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-020">SCOPE: Endpoint values MUST reference the pinned model deployment versions per §7.4 (gpt-4o 2024-08-06, gpt-4o-mini 2024-07-18, text-embedding-3-large v1).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">SCOPE: Registers in L2 control-plane DI container, NOT the BFF.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036">SCOPE: 3-level idempotency (MessageId + Redis lock + deterministic key h12c-{customerId}-{tenancyModel}-{endpointHash}).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §4D I3">SCOPE: All Cosmos + Dataverse operations use partition-key / alternate-key predicates; no cross-partition drift.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: For Model 1, metering-layer wiring integrates with task 077 (per-tenant token metering); Model 1 rows carry a metering-attribution tenantId field.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>H12c runtime references handler with Model 1/2 tier branch</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-004-job-contract.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-020-versioning.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-036-background-job-infrastructure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/jobs.md</file>
